// XFAIL: DF-270e — a PRIMITIVE TYPE NAME written as a ZERO-ARGUMENT call is an
// internal compiler error ("Undefined function: UInt8") where every other
// nonsense call is a clean diagnostic.
//
// Found by the fuzz lane (seed 1, index 136: `yield_now` -> `UInt8` in
// `channel_receive_in_main.saw`), and PRE-EXISTING — it has nothing to do with
// the `Byte` alias that reshuffled the corpus onto it. The mechanism is the
// arity: a call on a name that resolves to a primitive PSEUDO-STRUCT reaches
// the struct-initialization path only when it has arguments, so `UInt8(5)`
// lands on "struct initialization requires named arguments" while `UInt8()`
// falls through to function lookup and raises instead of reporting.
//
// The whole family is affected — `Int`, `UInt`, `Int8`…`Int64`,
// `UInt8`…`UInt64`, `Float`, `Bool`, `String`, all identical. `Never()` is
// clean (it is not registered as an extendable pseudo-struct), and so is
// `Byte()` over the design-250 alias, which reports "`Byte` is a type alias and
// is constructed from exactly one value, but 0 were given".
//
// The intended behaviour is stated as an ABSENCE rather than a wording, since
// the diagnostic this should produce has not been designed: whatever it says,
// it must not be an ICE.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-ABSENT: internal compiler error

func main() {
    UInt8()
    Int()
    String()
}
